{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1835 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2b468d1415338c777f907b7036fd49cbe7d3ab357a2b2985fcb8bb3eef829d4b" :edb/db-before-t 1834 :edb/db-after-t 1835 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535147 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:01:06.861Z" 13194139535147 true] [17592186105848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333825 13194139535147 true] [17592186105848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333832 13194139535147 true] [17592186105849 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333818 13194139535147 true] [17592186105849 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333836 13194139535147 true] [17592186105849 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333839 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333819 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1089 "q-20701" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056069/assets/d1318686a66856057fb04027ac52ff20266e628a498458b283ee93df1e4294eb.png)\n\nFind the total area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y={e}^{-|x|}$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above." 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1113 #uuid "72e381da-a408-5767-8a79-4cc713ab2c85" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333818 1145 "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{x}{|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{0}-{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =1+0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand ${e}^{-|x|}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-|x|}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333820 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333821 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333822 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333823 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333824 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1041 "selection" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333822 13194139535147 true] [17592186333819 1110 #uuid "f9a8336c-8d99-5fd1-b59c-07b5b5e9f477" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333820 1034 "3" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333820 1111 #uuid "3d18f346-7e92-5bdb-abd0-77ba69d1f332" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333821 1034 "7" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333821 1111 #uuid "5649faba-09af-5e19-8339-7fa2bd4013e7" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333822 1034 "2" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333822 1111 #uuid "940343d5-6e7e-5084-8b12-1e95728e0b65" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333823 1034 "6" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333823 1111 #uuid "16183522-8bb1-5238-a2cb-bd47c023f219" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333824 1034 "4" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333824 1111 #uuid "b4664283-1341-582e-94c0-76f79c2c1d79" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333826 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1089 "q-20789" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1113 #uuid "3151b187-7ba7-51ad-ac17-f4aeb94c10de" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333825 1145 "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u=2+{x}^{4}$,  then $\\text{d}u=4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{4}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the first of the improper integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({-\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{4}}|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2+0}-\\frac{1}{2+{a}^{4}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **odd** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{(2+{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333827 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333828 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333829 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333830 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333831 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1041 "selection" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333830 13194139535147 true] [17592186333826 1110 #uuid "189df852-c468-5647-8daa-2cc008546104" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333827 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333827 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333827 1111 #uuid "6aed9c37-d74a-5aa1-8fff-8329b2fe065e" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333828 1034 "The integral is divergent" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535147 true] [17592186333828 1111 #uuid "7f1a2368-159a-50e0-b5a8-74e49c06bdb0" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333829 1034 "1" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333829 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333829 1111 #uuid "c4ba3430-96d6-54da-8eca-e9f7c54975a0" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333830 1034 "0" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333830 1111 #uuid "50e013d7-fc24-5dee-bd39-d65d624f68e5" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333831 1034 "-1" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333831 1111 #uuid "6d1f64b8-66eb-55e1-aab0-7f61d89252c8" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333833 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1089 "q-347615" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1113 #uuid "8e60192a-b913-5728-aef5-1ff3e9342621" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333832 1145 "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25} & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{(x/5)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}\\cdot 5{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{3\\pi }{10}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{10}+\\frac{3\\pi }{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333834 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333835 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1041 "field-1" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333834 13194139535147 true] [17592186333833 1110 #uuid "6d9eebbf-ff83-5c0f-94a9-658a6f43dd41" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333834 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi}{5}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333834 1111 #uuid "ea483fb0-880f-56a3-8cea-48a0eb0d4a11" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333835 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{5}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333835 1111 #uuid "19af8603-274e-5fc8-80ed-e1dbe0c485fd" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333837 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1089 "q-351605" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1100 "Find the total area $A$ of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}$ and the $x$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1113 #uuid "e3328082-de37-543e-aded-b2717939c17f" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333836 1145 "Let's sketch a graph of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056069/assets/2b7b85dd8894c73275816a8ee08a8c8a41fb41a327d20ed7bedc489f7e2e55ff.png)\n\nWe find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the first of these integrals:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u={x}^{2}$, then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{u}{3}))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}))|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{\\pi }{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333838 13194139535147 true] [17592186333837 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535147 true] [17592186333837 1041 "field-1" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333837 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333838 13194139535147 true] [17592186333837 1110 #uuid "e26f3a22-bca2-51f8-a42d-7a26cc23dffb" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333838 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333838 1111 #uuid "b47c68c9-f96e-5f1e-9485-00dfdf1ac9e1" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333840 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1089 "q-5966" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14056069/assets/dd286aa5384dae22d8fff4bb29799078547064926697d71b0b0ca8739641408f.png)\n\nFind the total area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above." 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1113 #uuid "00ca25d1-569a-59b9-b8d5-e651fc67373e" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333839 1145 "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{6}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{x}{6}|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{a}{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\frac{a}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333841 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333842 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333843 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333844 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333845 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1041 "selection" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333842 13194139535147 true] [17592186333840 1110 #uuid "a43314a5-2d1d-5846-a608-d79041384b22" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333841 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333841 1111 #uuid "f4c8e5dc-8208-54f7-9dbd-a127bded25de" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333842 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333842 1111 #uuid "b2edc483-9775-564d-824f-42b728521162" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333843 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333843 1111 #uuid "d5937bbc-90d6-54f3-aec9-c9fcb207806e" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333844 1034 "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333844 1111 #uuid "55c392b9-0605-565d-9646-101ba70e8a6f" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333845 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" 13194139535147 true] [17592186333845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535147 true] [17592186333845 1111 #uuid "b220b1bb-be34-5e7d-a635-4e5564304a87" 13194139535147 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-20701" 17